## Original Content
Georgia-Pacific cut its SSPs by 80%. Here’s what it learned about supply-side control.

## Summary
Georgia-Pacific reduced its supply-side platforms by 80%, focusing on supply-side control in programmatic advertising. The company learned key insights about managing supply effectively, shifting away from demand-side strategies.

## Key Points
- Georgia-Pacific cut its SSPs by 80% to streamline operations.
- The company shifted focus from demand-side to supply-side control in programmatic advertising.
- Learned that supply-side management can lead to improved efficiency and better outcomes.
- Optimizing supply provides valuable insights for programmatic strategies.


